{
  "strategy": "Answer from scratch by locating the visual math setup that shows the first two glass-stacking cases, retrieving a few candidate frames around that setup, and then reading the heights/relationships from the diagram or on-screen text to compute the height of one glass and map it to the closest option.",
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "tool": "temporal_grounder",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "video",
        "query": "visual puzzle or diagram showing stacked glasses with heights labeled for the first two cases"
      },
      "purpose": "Localize the interval where the answer-critical diagram with the first two cases is shown before attempting frame-level reading.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "tool": "frame_retriever",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "video",
        "query": null,
        "timestamps": [
          "<STEP_1:segments[0].start>",
          "<STEP_1:segments[0].end>",
          "<STEP_1:segments[1].start>"
        ],
        "num_frames": 3
      },
      "purpose": "Sample candidate frames from the top localized intervals to capture the full puzzle state and avoid relying on a single possibly partial or explanation-phase frame.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "tool": "ocr",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_2:frames>",
        "timestamp": null
      },
      "purpose": "Read any visible numbers, labels, or measurement text associated with the first two glass cases.",
      "depends_on": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "tool": "dense_captioner",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "video",
        "start_time": "<STEP_1:segments[0].start>",
        "end_time": "<STEP_1:segments[0].end>",
        "granularity": "frame"
      },
      "purpose": "Provide structured visual context for the bounded puzzle interval in case the key evidence is conveyed by object arrangement rather than clean OCR alone, e.g., number of glasses in each case and how they are stacked.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "refinement_instructions": "Build the first trace from the new evidence only. First identify which retrieved frame/span actually shows the original puzzle state with the first two cases, not a later explanation overlay. Use OCR as authoritative for any visible numeric heights or labels. Use dense_captioner only to establish the visual arrangement of the cases (such as how many glasses appear in each stack and whether the second case adds one more glass), not to invent exact numbers. Then derive the height of one glass algebraically from the first two cases: translate each displayed case into an equation, solve for the single-glass height, and explicitly compare the computed value against options A–E. If OCR on one frame is partial, reconcile across the candidate frames from step 2 and cite the frame-level evidence that contains the complete measurements. Update the final answer to the option matching the computed value; if the computed value is approximate, explain the closest-option mapping."}
